nal data":"none","postal addresses":"none","source":"ultrachat","toxicity":"none"},"text":"<|im_start|>system\nYou are a helpful assistant.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nWrite a step-by-step instructional guide that includes all the necessary ingredients, measurements, equipment, and procedures to make fluffy and soft dinner rolls with clear and concise language and organized layout for ease of following.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nHow to Make Fluffy and Soft Dinner Rolls:\n\nIngredients:\n- 4 cups of all-purpose flour\n- 2 tsp of instant yeast\n- 1/4 cup of granulated sugar\n- 1 tsp of salt\n- 1/4 cup of unsalted butter, melted\n- 1 cup of warm milk (110°F – 115°F)\n- 2 eggs\n\nEquipment:\n- Mixing bowl\n- Measuring cups\n- Measuring spoons\n- Rubber spatula\n- Stand mixer with dough hook attachment\n- Pastry brush\n- Baking sheet\n- Parchment paper\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. In a bowl, combine the flour, instant yeast, sugar, and salt.\n\n2. In another bowl, whisk together the warm milk, melted butter, and eggs.\n\n3. Add the wet ingredients to the dry mixture and mix until well combined. If using a stand mixer, use the dough hook attachment and mix on low speed for 5-7 minutes. If mixing by hand, stir with a spatula until a dough forms.\n\n4. Transfer the dough to a lightly floured surface and knead by hand for an additional 5-7 minutes until smooth and elastic.\n\n5. Shape the dough into a ball and place it in a greased bowl. Cover with a damp towel and let it rise in a warm place for 1-2 hours or until doubled in size.\n\n6. Preheat the oven to 375°F.\n\n7. Divide the dough into equal portions (approximately 12-16 pieces) and shape into rolls. Place the rolls on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper.\n\n8. Cover the rolls with a damp towel and let them rise for an additional 30 minutes.\n\n9. In a small bowl, whisk an egg with a tablespoon of water. Use a pastry brush to brush the rolls with the egg wash.\n\n10. Bake for 15-20 minutes or until golden brown.\n\n11. Remove from oven and let the rolls cool on a wire rack.\n\n12. Serve warm with butter and enjoy!\n\nTips:\n- Make sure the milk is not too hot, as it can kill the yeast. The ideal temperature is between 110°F – 115°F.\n- Use room temperature eggs to help the dough rise better.\n- Cover the rolls with a damp towel during both rising times to prevent them from drying out.\n- If the rolls are browning too quickly, cover them loosely with aluminum foil halfway through baking.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nThanks for the clear instructions on how to make fluffy and soft dinner rolls! Can you suggest any variations to add some flavor to the rolls? Maybe some herbs or cheese?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nSure, here are some variations you can try to add more flavor to your dinner rolls:\n\n1. Garlic and Parmesan - mix some finely grated Parmesan cheese and minced garlic into the dough before shaping it into rolls. You can also brush the rolls with garlic butter and sprinkle more Parmesan cheese on top before baking.\n\n2. Rosemary and Sea Salt - add some dried rosemary to the dough while mixing, and sprinkle some coarse sea salt o","tokens":["<","|","im","_","start","|>","system","\n","You"," are"," a"," helpful"," assistant",".<","|","im","_","end","|>","\n","<","|","im","_","start","|>","user","\n","Write"," a"," step","-","by","-","step"," instruction","al"," guide"," that"," includes"," all"," the"," necessary"," ingredients",","," measurements",","," equipment",","," and"," procedures"," to"," make"," fl","uffy"," and"," soft"," dinner"," rolls"," with"," clear"," and"," concise"," language"," and"," organized"," layout"," for"," ease"," of"," following",".<","|","im","_","end","|>","\n","<","|","im","_","start","|>","ass","istant","\n","How"," to"," Make"," Fl","uffy"," and"," Soft"," D","inner"," Roll","s",":","\n","\n","In","g","redients",":","\n","-"," 4"," cups"," of"," all","-","purpose"," flour","\n","-"," 2"," tsp"," of"," instant"," yeast","\n",